        "body": "A small explicit root shortlist can lose the target yield even when its selection uses arbitrary coordinates and adapts within one input half. This change counts the actual successful product worlds without assuming uniform selected outputs, then applies the unchanged endpoint at prime-field Weierstrass subgroups. It separately analyzes tree representations for an already supplied tuple and identifies joint-query/overlapping-support interfaces that lie outside the independent-half bound. [pcc:unverified]\n\nThe six-field prospective plan, inherited-law floor and proof map precede three reusable laws in `Group.ShortlistCompletion`. Existing equal-fiber, kernel-cardinality, surjection and Sigma-count laws supply the proof; the partite instance uses the existing tuple-sum surjectivity. Actual-field assembly passes. Canonical gate001 audits215 theorems with0 failures and0 trusted-native exceptions; all3 named axiom prints use only standard axioms. No fresh checker or hosted pass is asserted. [pcc:unverified]\n\nThe report, DOT/SVG and visually inspected three-page PDF distinguish formal counts, hand probability/cost statements and unimplemented successors. PCC-20261116-d003a9 remains unverified, with nine attestation subjects; the five-row owner ledger is an exact prefix and all32 older claim subjects are unchanged. Original failed sources/logs remain. Source/prose whitespace check exits0; full archival check exits2 on original diagnostic spaces. No proof-limit, trust, inventory or linter policy changes. [pcc:unverified]\n\nPR20 landing/hosted-failure receipts and its queued autonomy/outcome accompany this substantive assessment. Consumer frozen-history conflicts stay separate. No numerical/native/qualification or paid execution. Joint construction, useful yield and full recovery/cost remain missing from the complete end-to-end criterion. [pcc:unverified]\n",
